==Strategy==
Essentially a nerfed down version of [[Vulcanizer (Deadly)|Vulcanizer]], the boss here has lower overall stats and is supported with weaker peons. However, due to the 4-star restrictions in place as well as the faster attack rate from the boss, this stage can be very threatening without the right units. [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]], who plays a crucial part in Vulcanizer, sees the same importance here. Although keep in mind, stalling will be a bit more difficult due to the presence of the squire rels disrupting your meatshield line.

Alternatively, you can use [[Cat God the Great (Special Cat)|Cat God the Great]] to great effect here, since the stage length is extremely short. Cat God can help cheese the stage if you don't have other options to do so, and if you use him, he can pin all enemies to the base, and destroy the enemy base with his Omni Strike while standing at a safe distance. Just make sure you protect him well.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]]: At Level 40 with one Defense UP Sm [[Cat Combo]], Haniwa Cat can survive a hit from Li'l Eraser Cat, making him perfect for stalling it. Haniwa can also stall the Squire Rel and Dagshund well since they are [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] too.
*[[Cat God the Great (Special Cat)|Cat God the Great]]: Since the stage is so short, he will almost always [[Knockback]] every enemy on the field. He can keep Li'l Eraser pinned to the base while also helping to kill the Owlbrows.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]]: When given both the [[Massive Damage]] and [[Special Abilities#Stat Enhancements|Attack Buff]] Talents, they can easily kill the Gory Dark waves in just seconds, making the stage much, much easier.
*[[Filibuster Cat X (Special Cat)|Filibuster Cat Y]]: This unit can outrange Li'l Eraser and freeze it, and while it is frozen, your attackers can deal a lot of damage.
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]: At level 54 (45 with max defense talent) Ramen can survive a single hit from Li'l Eraser. While, it's definitely worse than Haniwa due to its cooldown being more than double of Haniwa's it has the upside that it is able to deal decent chip damage with 4.4k+ dps at level 45.

